  "about": "The references around the world (ENGINE.md step 5, \"References around the world\"): the app's map over the world's own packs alone, world-refs (the tiles of these frames cut from a world release's parts by `packer world-refs`, and its globe), where no country has levels (the camera's WORLD_UNDER), as the phone draws it (every effect) at the frame below: the target at cy of its height from the top, straight down unless pitched, north up unless a bearing is given. A frame with a time is drawn at that instant in its zone (CoreMoment's live moment), the others at a moment of the port's. likeness/WorldPackRefs.kt's WorldPackRefsTest draws them on lavapipe in world.yml's refs job (a frame that cannot be decoded or drawn fails it) and holds the engine to the current version's frames once a version holds them, over the world they are of (the version's world, the release the refs job names in ATLAS_WORLD_REFS_RELEASE): another world's data draws other pixels with the same engine, so its frames are only proposed. A deliberate change is a new version, its frames from the refs job's proposal (the report's world-refs/world-refs.json).",
